comments.content:
This check is placed in the wrong branch. In this `else` branch `item` comes from `it->findItem(command)` where `it` is a direct child of `toolBar`, so `item` can never be `toolBar`. The path Coverity 513838 actually refers to is the branch above:
```cpp
if (ToolBarItem* item = toolBar->findItem(command)) {
    toolBar->removeItem(item);
    delete item;
}
```
`ToolBarItem::findItem()` returns `this` when the name matches, and the root toolbar created in `Workbench::setupToolBars()` has an empty command name (`new ToolBarItem` without `setCommand()`). So a manipulator returning `{"remove": ""}` makes `item == toolBar`, and `delete toolBar` destroys the whole toolbar tree; the caller (`Workbench::activate()`) then passes the freed pointer to `ToolBarManager::getInstance()->setup(tb)` — use-after-free. The guard should be moved into that `if` branch (and the same reasoning applies to the analogous `append` branch, where `toolBar->findItem(itemName)` may also return `toolBar`).

